    "policyNotes": [
        {
            "topic": "Muslim festival dates",
            "text": "This circular does not carry the '(*)' asterisk-marking convention used in later years' circulars for Muslim festivals dependent on moon-sighting (Id-ul-Fitr, Id-ul-Zuha, Jamat-Ul-Vida, etc.); no separate moon-sighting contingency clause is present in this circular or its addendum."
        },
        {
            "topic": "Restricted Holiday option deadline",
            "text": "For availing Restricted holidays (from para 2.2 and from para 2.4), concerned employees shall have to exercise their option by 31st January 2020 and obtain approval of their controlling officer before availing the same."
        },
        {
            "topic": "Compensatory Off",
            "text": "An employee, including an executive, who is not spared to avail a Closed/Public/Festival/Restricted holiday is entitled to one day's compensatory-off in lieu, within the calendar year and within two months of the date on which the holiday falls due, with prior approval of the controlling officer. An industrial non-executive employee (Works & Non-Works) who cannot be spared, or does not want to avail the Closed/Public holiday(s) on Republic Day, May Day, Independence Day or Mahatma Gandhi's Birthday, has the option of claiming Compensatory Off within the calendar year or extra wages instead; this option is also available if any of these four holidays coincides with their weekly off (excluding Sunday) -- in case of a Sunday weekly-off, only Compensatory Off is admissible. All executives and non-executive employees (following the industrial pattern of holidays) may be allowed one day's compensatory-off for each Public/Closed holiday coinciding with their weekly off (including Sunday)."
        },
        {
            "topic": "Proportionate RH for new joiners",
            "text": "Employees joining services of the company during the calendar year will be entitled for proportionate Festival/Restricted Holiday(s) to be calculated on half-yearly or quarterly basis with reference to their joining date, as the case may be."
        },
        {
            "topic": "Non-executive Trainee entitlement",
            "text": "Non-executive Trainees (Category D) are entitled to 05 Closed/Public Holidays and 04 Restricted Holidays, as admissible to industrial non-executives per Clause 1.0 and 2.2 of the original circular. This entitlement was fixed before the addendum dated 28.12.2019 was issued; the addendum's 4 extra Restricted Holiday options were extended explicitly only to industrial non-executive employees (Category C), not to Trainees, so Trainees' RH pool remains the original 33-holiday list, not the addendum-expanded 37-holiday pool available to Category C."
        },
        {
            "topic": "Addendum: extra RH options for Category C",
            "text": "Per the addendum circular dated 28.12.2019 (Circular Sl. No. 2019/41/1), industrial non-executive employees (Category C) can additionally choose from 4 more Restricted Holidays -- Idu'l Fitr (25th May), Durgapuja-Vijaya Dashami (26th October), Guru Nanak's Birthday (30th November), and Christmas Day (25th December) -- on top of the 33-holiday list already indicated at pt.2.2 of the original circular. This does not change Category C's quota, which remains 4 Restricted Holidays for the year; it only expands the pool of holidays they may choose those 4 from."
        }
    ]
}